  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>mape</keyword>
  <short_description>Mean absolute percentage error.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>E = mape(F, A)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>E = mape(F, A, dim)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>E = mape(F, A, 'all')</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>E = mape(..., nanflag)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>E = mape(..., 'Weights', w)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>F</param_name>
      <param_description>forecast values: a single or double array.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>A</param_name>
      <param_description>actual values: a single or double array compatible with <b>F</b>.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>dim</param_name>
      <param_description>dimension to operate along, or <b>'all'</b>.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>nanflag</param_name>
      <param_description><b>'includenan'</b> (default) or <b>'omitnan'</b>.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>w</param_name>
      <param_description>weights given with <b>'Weights'</b>: a vector along <b>dim</b> or an array of the size of the data.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>E</param_name>
      <param_description>the mean absolute percentage error along <b>dim</b>, in percent.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>E = mape(F, A)</b> returns <b>100 * mean(abs((A - F) ./ A))</b> along the first dimension whose size is not 1. A zero actual value with a nonzero error gives <b>Inf</b>.</p>
    <p>The dimension, <b>'all'</b>, <b>nanflag</b> and <b>'Weights'</b> options work as for <b>rmse</b>.</p>
  </description>
